  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably mild and dry weather will continue \nuntil late Wednesday or Wednesday Night prior to a few periods \nof showers preceding and accompanying a cold frontal passage. \nCooler and a return to mainly dry conditions will follow for \nFriday through Sunday.\n\nLatest satellite loop and regional obs showing lower-based\naltocu advecting ENE across the western half of the CWA with\nsome light refl returns from virga near the Western edge of our\nCWA. \n\n09z temps in the upper 40s to low 50s were as much as 10-13 deg\nF above normal across the SW zones where the cloud cover is the\nthickest, while some periods of thin cirrus across the North and\nEast has allowed the mercury to into the upper 30s to low 40s\n(4-5F above normal).\n\nThe close proximity of the large, 1032 MB surface high located\njust east of KACY will keep winds light from the SE or South.\n\nA sprinkle isn't out of the question over the North tonight \n- much like the very small and brief shower they had two nights \nago. We'll keep the forecast at 0 PoP since there is no risk of \n0.01\" accumulating. That isn't great news for northern PA where \nBFD only accumulated 0.85\" through all of Oct, and is currently \non a run of 14 straight days without measurable (0.01\") rain.\n\nUpper level ridging builds back into the region for the first \nhalf of this week, helping to prolong our dry stretch and \nkeeping high temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above normal for much\nof week followed by a moderate cooldown of 8-15 deg F in the \nThursday to Sunday period.\n\nHighs in the lower 70s are in store for all but the higher \nelevations on Wed.\n\nChances for widespread rainfall return for the second half of\nthe week. Very late Wed or Wed night is the earliest anyone \nwill see precip as a complex system develops over the middle of \nthe country. There is still a lot of uncertainty regarding the \nevolution of the upper air pattern and phasing of energy aloft \nthat will decide the development and progression of this system.\nThe more weighted/favored (per WPC) ECMWF solution yields only \na brief 12-18hr window of precip as the cold front moves through\n(longer in the eastern half of the CWA than over the west) Wed \nnight and Thurs. Cold air under a sharp trough could make the \nfirst part of the weekend a little chilly and damp with \ninstability showers.",
